      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the first five prime numbers is divided by the sixth prime number, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first five prime numbers:\n   - The first prime number is \\(2\\).\n   - The second prime number is \\(3\\).\n   - The third prime number is \\(5\\).\n   - The fourth prime number is \\(7\\).\n   - The fifth prime number is \\(11\\).\n\n2. Calculate the sum of these prime numbers:\n   \\[\n   2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\n   \\]\n\n3. Perform the addition:\n   \\[\n   2 + 3 = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5 + 5 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   10 + 7 = 17\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   17 + 11 = 28\n   \\]\n\n4. Identify the sixth prime number:\n   - The sixth prime number is \\(13\\).\n\n5. Now, need to find the remainder when \\(28\\) is divided by \\(13\\):\n   \\[\n   28 \\div 13 = 2 \\text{ with a remainder of } 2\n   \\]\n\n6. Confirm the calculation:\n   - \\(28 \\div 13 = 2\\) with a remainder of \\(2\\).\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime number is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
